[{:db/id 17592186129161 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-00fd1a7d-44b2-529b-bcff-08a778520166"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-00fd1a7d-44b2-529b-bcff-08a778520166" :question/id #uuid "00fd1a7d-44b2-529b-bcff-08a778520166" :question/math-academy-id "q-71586" :question/problem "Which of the following describes the level surfaces of the function $f(x,y,z)=(x+y+z)^{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "The level surfaces of the function $f(x,y,z)$ are given by the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & =c \\\\ (x+y+z)^{2} & =c \\\\ x+y+z & =\\pm \\sqrt{c} \\\\ x+y+z\\pm \\sqrt{c} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $f(x,y,z)$ can't be negative. Therefore, we get a family of planes:\n\n$$\nx+y+z\\pm \\sqrt{c}=0,\\,c\\in [0,\\infty ).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-44405f81-ea2c-5ec0-9035-361601af3ea6"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-44405f81-ea2c-5ec0-9035-361601af3ea6" :answer-field/id #uuid "44405f81-ea2c-5ec0-9035-361601af3ea6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-d11d59ab-ca32-5bdd-988e-9f236a634db6" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c52cd181-65a2-5882-be1e-55e40ba886c7" "answer-d11d59ab-ca32-5bdd-988e-9f236a634db6" "answer-90d9747b-5cb9-522d-836f-d3553c78f3a4" "answer-b986da89-36d0-55a1-8a48-c9bd757d18db" "answer-e4bedb04-7179-51c0-917b-125bf66e2a73"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c52cd181-65a2-5882-be1e-55e40ba886c7" :answer/id #uuid "c52cd181-65a2-5882-be1e-55e40ba886c7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "A family of hyperboloids of one sheet: ${c}^{2}{x}^{2}+{c}^{2}{y}^{2}-{c}^{2}{z}^{2}=1$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d11d59ab-ca32-5bdd-988e-9f236a634db6" :answer/id #uuid "d11d59ab-ca32-5bdd-988e-9f236a634db6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "A family of planes: $x+y+z\\pm \\sqrt{c}=0$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-90d9747b-5cb9-522d-836f-d3553c78f3a4" :answer/id #uuid "90d9747b-5cb9-522d-836f-d3553c78f3a4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "A family of planes: $x+y-{z}^{2}-\\sqrt{c}=0$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b986da89-36d0-55a1-8a48-c9bd757d18db" :answer/id #uuid "b986da89-36d0-55a1-8a48-c9bd757d18db" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "A family of spheres: ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}={c}^{2}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e4bedb04-7179-51c0-917b-125bf66e2a73" :answer/id #uuid "e4bedb04-7179-51c0-917b-125bf66e2a73" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "A family of surfaces given by $z=(x+y+c)^{2}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186129162 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-595252cd-1afe-5f16-ae97-13c476966ff1" "question-ef96fb6f-8651-5bcd-8700-e66e3e1a4bf5"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-595252cd-1afe-5f16-ae97-13c476966ff1" :question/id #uuid "595252cd-1afe-5f16-ae97-13c476966ff1" :question/math-academy-id "q-71594" :question/problem "Find the equation of the level surface for the function $f(x,y,z)=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-{z}^{2}}$ that passes through the point $P(2,\\sqrt{5},3).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the value of the function at $P$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(2,\\sqrt{5},3) & =\\frac{(2)^{2}}{2(2)^{2}+(\\sqrt{5})^{2}-(3)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{4} \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that the level surfaces for the function $f(x,y,z)$ are given by the equation\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)=c.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we're interested in $c=1.$ So, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & =c \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{2{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-{z}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =2{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-{z}^{2} \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-{z}^{2} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the level surface that passes through the point $P(2,\\sqrt{5},3)$ is the surface ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-{z}^{2}=0.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e10467a3-d69e-5402-aad3-4b64333f090a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e10467a3-d69e-5402-aad3-4b64333f090a" :answer-field/id #uuid "e10467a3-d69e-5402-aad3-4b64333f090a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-7161819e-ecce-539e-a7d9-dd1392ee66bd" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f1e2ddba-6b1f-50a3-8f82-6a0e5406e403" "answer-bf6e5c59-e63b-5d91-add0-3fc776b81f35" "answer-f41b80f9-1883-5d0f-a39d-6bf74d468448" "answer-7161819e-ecce-539e-a7d9-dd1392ee66bd" "answer-fab3e1ad-3d44-56bd-8a1c-54fb07d88d5c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f1e2ddba-6b1f-50a3-8f82-6a0e5406e403" :answer/id #uuid "f1e2ddba-6b1f-50a3-8f82-6a0e5406e403" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-{z}^{2}=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bf6e5c59-e63b-5d91-add0-3fc776b81f35" :answer/id #uuid "bf6e5c59-e63b-5d91-add0-3fc776b81f35" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-{z}^{2}=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f41b80f9-1883-5d0f-a39d-6bf74d468448" :answer/id #uuid "f41b80f9-1883-5d0f-a39d-6bf74d468448" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-z=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7161819e-ecce-539e-a7d9-dd1392ee66bd" :answer/id #uuid "7161819e-ecce-539e-a7d9-dd1392ee66bd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-{z}^{2}=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fab3e1ad-3d44-56bd-8a1c-54fb07d88d5c" :answer/id #uuid "fab3e1ad-3d44-56bd-8a1c-54fb07d88d5c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}-{z}^{2}=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-ef96fb6f-8651-5bcd-8700-e66e3e1a4bf5" :question/id #uuid "ef96fb6f-8651-5bcd-8700-e66e3e1a4bf5" :question/math-academy-id "q-129189" :question/problem "Find the equation of the level surface for the function $f(x,y,z)={y}^{2}-{x}^{2}-z$ that passes through the point $P(0,-2,4).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the value of the function at $P:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0,2,4) & ={2}^{2}-{0}^{2}-4 \\\\  & =4-0-4 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that the level surfaces for the function $f(x,y,z)$ are given by the equation\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)=c.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we're interested in $c=0.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & =c \\\\ {y}^{2}-{x}^{2}-z & =0 \\\\ z & ={y}^{2}-{x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the level surface that passes through the point $P(0,-2,4)$ is the hyperbolic paraboloid $z={y}^{2}-{x}^{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c684e12d-e352-5e5e-a84d-c529f9dea534"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c684e12d-e352-5e5e-a84d-c529f9dea534" :answer-field/id #uuid "c684e12d-e352-5e5e-a84d-c529f9dea534" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-075b7e9b-145b-5c05-9d44-d25bd4906906" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2ebb8400-2445-5e48-a715-3c49140534aa" "answer-075b7e9b-145b-5c05-9d44-d25bd4906906" "answer-3e1d8da5-60a8-5dd3-b8c1-c0a4396407a6" "answer-d72a7a8d-f6c0-55af-9c80-47300b8e44cf" "answer-f658e47e-1f73-55ca-b61e-916ac3975ae3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2ebb8400-2445-5e48-a715-3c49140534aa" :answer/id #uuid "2ebb8400-2445-5e48-a715-3c49140534aa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z={x}^{2}-{y}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-075b7e9b-145b-5c05-9d44-d25bd4906906" :answer/id #uuid "075b7e9b-145b-5c05-9d44-d25bd4906906" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z={y}^{2}-{x}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3e1d8da5-60a8-5dd3-b8c1-c0a4396407a6" :answer/id #uuid "3e1d8da5-60a8-5dd3-b8c1-c0a4396407a6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z={y}^{2}-{x}^{2}+2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d72a7a8d-f6c0-55af-9c80-47300b8e44cf" :answer/id #uuid